2. In these Regulations, unless the context otherwise requires —
“appointed date” means 1 October 2016;
“Former IDA” has the same meaning as in section 87 of the IMDA Act;
“Former MDA” has the same meaning as in section 87 of the IMDA Act;
“IMDA Act” means the Info-communications Media Development Authority Act 2016 (Act 22 of 2016);
“principal Act” means any Act (except a repealed Act) that, immediately before the appointed date, authorised the Former IDA (or any of its employees) or the Former MDA (or any of its employees) to perform any function under that Act;
“repealed Act” means the Info-communications Development Authority of Singapore Act (Cap. 137A) or the Media Development Authority of Singapore Act (Cap. 172);
“Section 16 Notification” means the Media Development Authority of Singapore (Regulated Persons) Notification 2003 (G.N. No. S 176/2003) made by the Minister under section 16(3) of the Media Development Authority of Singapore Act in force immediately before the appointed date;
“Section 21 Notification” means the Media Development Authority of Singapore (Regulated Persons) (Dominant and Non‑dominant Positions) Notification 2003 (G.N. No. S 180/2003) made by the Former MDA under section 21(4) of the Media Development Authority of Singapore Act in force immediately before the appointed day;
“transferred IDA employee” means an employee of the Former IDA who is transferred to the Authority on the appointed date under section 84(1) of the IMDA Act;
“transferred IDA function” means any function discharged by the Info-communications Media Development Authority Designate Wing of the Info-communications Authority of Singapore on the eve of the appointed date;
“transferred MDA employee” means an employee of the Former MDA who is transferred to the Authority on the appointed date under section 84(1) of the IMDA Act.
